From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] imcontextwayland: forget a context that loses focus before text input is bound

A text field focused as a window opens, and destroyed before the Wayland
text-input manager is bound, left the input method's current context
pointing at freed memory: focus_out looked the context up through a helper
that returns nothing until text input exists, so it never cleared it. The
next text-input event dereferenced it and the application crashed.

--- a/gtk/gtkimcontextwayland.c
+++ b/gtk/gtkimcontextwayland.c
@@ -813,11 +813,19 @@
   GtkIMContextWayland *self = GTK_IM_CONTEXT_WAYLAND (context);
   GtkIMContextWaylandGlobal *global;
 
-  global = gtk_im_context_wayland_get_global (self);
-  if (global == NULL)
-    return;
-
-  if (global->focused)
+  if (self->widget == NULL)
+    return;
+
+  /* Not gtk_im_context_wayland_get_global(): it returns NULL until the
+   * text-input manager is bound. A context focused before then, and
+   * destroyed before then, stayed global->current after it was freed, and
+   * the next text-input event used it. */
+  global = g_object_get_data (G_OBJECT (gtk_widget_get_display (self->widget)),
+                              "gtk-im-context-wayland-global");
+  if (global == NULL || global->current != context)
+    return;
+
+  if (global->text_input != NULL && global->focused)
     disable (self, global);
 
   global->current = NULL;
